{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790274559,"nonce":"aw/dkKb5pl+8xFdxE9IY4AQwHyg=","title":"Python: exception constructors on raise arms are not cold, so accessors with a raise path stay call-bearing","message":"The inliner treats a callee as call-bearing only by calls on blocks that reach its return without a cold call (4c42cdd5). Python's raise arms call a plain exception constructor such as IndexError$new, which is not marked cold, so the arm is not recognised as an error path and the callee keeps its calls: with ZYNTAX_TRACE_INLINE=1 a Box.get with an IndexError raise path is refused ('Box$get refuses IndexError$new (callee with calls outside a loop)', 'once refuses Box$get (callee with calls outside a loop, callee insts: 32)'). Lua's zl_index_nil/zl_annotate and zb_fatal arms are cold and are recognised.\n\nDirection: the frontend marks the helper a raise arm ends in as cold (the call that sets the pending exception, or the constructor when its result is only raised), so blocks_leading_to_cold sees the arm.","files":null}]}